      "message": "doing 64-bit computations is pretty inefficient on Cortex-M0,\nand probably useless here (since us is 32-bit).\n\nYou can do at least something like :\nuint32_t t0, elapsed;\n\nt0 \u003d __hw_clock_source_read();\ndo {\n        elapsed \u003d  __hw_clock_source_read() - t0;\n        if (elapsed \u003e\u003d us)\n               break;\n\tevt |\u003d task_wait_event(us - elapsed);\n} while (!(evt \u0026 TASK_EVENT_TIMER))\n\nI let you verify again that all integer rollover in my example are correct. \n\nIMO the following was good enough (even if less precise) but as you want...\nuint32_t t0 \u003d __hw_clock_source_read();\n\ndo {\n\tevt |\u003d task_wait_event(us);\n} while (!(evt \u0026 TASK_EVENT_TIMER) \u0026\u0026 ((__hw_clock_source_read() - t0) \u003c us));",
